   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12. Pigeonhole Principle in Hashing\n",
    "The Pigeonhole Principle states that if $n$ items (pigeons) are placed into $m$ slots (pigeonholes) and $n > m$, then at least one slot contains at least $\\lceil n/m \\rceil$ items.\n",
    "For $n=50$ items hashed into $m=40$ buckets:\n",
    "- At least one bucket contains at least $\\lceil 50/40 \\rceil = 2$ items.\n",
    "- The minimum number of collisions (instances where a slot is already occupied) is $n - m = 50 - 40 = 10$ collisions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Theoretical answer verified."
   ]
  },
