   "source": [
    "### 13. Weisfeiler-Lehman Isomorphism Test\n",
    "The WL-1 test colors nodes iteratively based on their current color and the multiset of their neighbors' colors. Graphs that result in different color distributions are non-isomorphic."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def wl_1_step(adj, colors):\n",
    "    new_colors = []\n",
    "    for i in range(len(adj)):\n",
    "        neighbors = sorted([colors[j] for j in range(len(adj)) if adj[i, j] == 1])\n",
    "        new_colors.append(hash((colors[i], tuple(neighbors))))\n",
    "    # remap to small integers\n",
    "    unique = sorted(list(set(new_colors)))\n",
    "    color_map = {c: idx for idx, c in enumerate(unique)}\n",
    "    return [color_map[c] for c in new_colors]\n",
    "\n",
    "adj = np.array([[0, 1], [1, 0]])\n",
    "colors = [1, 1]\n",
    "print(\"WL Colors after 1 step:\", wl_1_step(adj, colors))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 14. Cartesian Product and Relations\n",
    "For sets $A$ and $B$, the Cartesian product size is $|A \\times B| = |A| \\times |B| = 2 \\times 3 = 6$.\n",
    "A binary relation is any subset of $A \\times B$. The number of possible subsets is $2^{|A \\times B|} = 2^6 = 64$ relations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import itertools\n",
    "A = {1, 2}\n",
    "B = {'a', 'b', 'c'}\n",
    "prod = list(itertools.product(A, B))\n",
    "print(\"Cartesian Product:\", prod)\n",
    "print(\"Number of relations:\", 2**len(prod))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 15. Graph Laplacians for Image Segmentation\n",
    "An image grid can be represented as a graph where nodes are pixels and edges connect neighboring pixels. The weights of the edges reflect the similarity (in intensity/color) between pixels.\n",
    "We can perform spectral clustering on this graph to segment the image. Here is a toy 1D image $[10, 11, 12, 100, 101, 102]$ segmented using the Laplacian."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pixels = np.array([10.0, 11.0, 12.0, 100.0, 101.0, 102.0])\n",
    "n = len(pixels)\n",
    "A = np.zeros((n, n))\n",
    "for i in range(n-1):\n",
    "    diff = abs(pixels[i] - pixels[i+1])\n",
    "    weight = np.exp(-diff / 10.0)\n",
    "    A[i, i+1] = weight\n",
    "    A[i+1, i] = weight\n",
    "\n",
    "D = np.diag(np.sum(A, axis=1))\n",
    "L = D - A\n",
    "vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(L)\n",
    "fiedler = vecs[:, 1]\n",
    "print(\"Segmentation Partition:\", (fiedler > 0).astype(int))"
   ]
  }
 ]
